WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.069
So just reflect a minute: To get to the moon and back again required real

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:12.889
imagination, a goal to be set, but fundamentally, dynamic and

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:18.029
economy-wide interactions between
different actors to fuel investment in

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:22.980
innovation for a common purpose. So there was the challenge—the broad challenge

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.300
was at the time the Space Race and
Sputnik. The moon shot was very specific,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.990
but it required many different sectors
to innovate—not just aeronautics. There

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:34.710
was nutrition, and materials—there was
about 12 different sectors. And then what

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.980
government did was really transform its
instruments—like procurement and price

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.149
schemes and grants—to fuel that bottom-up experimentation. So over 300

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:45.930
projects in order to get to the moon, of
which many failed. So again, that kind of

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.980
risk-taking, really shared across many
different actors, but also, you know,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:01:02.969
bottom-up experimentation, also in
business, in order to reach a common goal.

